   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nCamille</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nYou continue to push the boundaries of analyses. I have never passed a data set with groups through\r\n<code>dht2</code>​, so I didn&#39;t know the answer to your question.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nPerforming an experiment with a data set that contains groups, and passing a fitted model object into\r\n<code>dht2</code>​, it appears <code>dht2</code>​ will only produce estimates of <b>\r\nindividual </b>density and abundance.  I&#39;ve submitted an issue for our programming team to address.</div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471909627000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2O76BKAQwckhmBLT_EK8Sf\">https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178</a></span></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"width:100%;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px;max-width:800px;min-width:424px\">\r\n<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"padding:12px 36px 12px 12px;width:100%;border-width:1px;border-style:solid;border-color:rgb(200,200,200);border-radius:2px\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr valign=\"top\" style=\"border-spacing:0px\">\r\n<td>\r\n<div style=\"margin-right:12px;min-height:120px;overflow:hidden;width:240px\">\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471909627000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2O76BKAQwckhmBLT_EK8Sf\"><img alt=\"\" style=\"display:block\" height=\"120\" width=\"240\" src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/KTcNGKOI-a-S7-GiSwUK3FOT9ifsJZeemDYm1-4VOtlfkKFXwnuQHBQ4B5adRuviBJQOPBKrWUZ56WNE6yCp_7j_BHfxGT6Deu8DlS-Y_a0OiuaayvyeklC2zRggwgm1C5dRL3cSQ7LulqYwreweupj98179dN44Pgk95O2qy6SeJmvF0zRR4ViJyqTNvTpdwDisgNCO-MGpa3DAWvuT=s0-d-e1-ft#https://opengraph.githubassets.com/0a6ffc6c94d5261ecdf5f42fa8b41ea7590e7a49b117da00735a1a01d5cec61a/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178\"></a></div>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width:100%\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:300;margin-right:8px;font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP Light&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px\">\r\n<a href=\"https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:var(--themePrimary)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/Distance/issues/178&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471909627000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2O76BKAQwckhmBLT_EK8Sf\">`dht2` cannot produce estimates of group density/abundance · Issue #178 · DistanceDevelopment/Distance</a></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;max-height:100px;color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif;margin-bottom:12px;margin-right:8px;overflow:hidden\">\r\nWhen given data for animals observed in groups, dht2 only produces estimates of individual density and abundance. It does not produce estimates of group density or abundance. data(&quot;ClusterExercise&quot;...</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;font-weight:400;color:rgb(166,166,166);font-family:&quot;wf_segoe-ui_normal&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Segoe WP&quot;,Tahoma,Arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<a href=\"http://github.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://github.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471909627000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08p2l4WF6mQiOqAYWisEWy\">github.com</a></div>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nThe work-around you propose (remove (or rename)) the size column will work as long as group size is not involved in the detection function modelling.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Camille Ollier &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ollie...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 23 February 2024 16:53<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [distance-sampling] d