     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<div>Hello,<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Out of curiosity, is it possible to get the abundance of clusters and individuals (including CV, se etc.) using the `dht2` function, similar to the `ds` function with summary?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nAlternatively, should I manually remove the &quot;size&quot; column if I want to estimate the abundance of clusters with all the associated information?<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI ask this question because I intend to compare the abundance of clusters and individuals.<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Thank you in advance</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\nBest regards,<br>\r\nCamille<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<p></p></div></div>"
